  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:


  With the coming of the spring season, Josh the gentle set out to quench 
his thirst for glory.  He failed in his attempt to cast an Oratory spell.
  In early summer, Josh the gentle moved into Pakistan (#2806) with his 
army.

  A host of savage warriors carried the banner of 
Josh the gentle Sevenhalf-eight into the Mountain province of Pakistan, held 
by Rutger.  Josh the gentle was in command of the invading armies.  The 
defenders were commanded by Rutger.  The armies were drawn up into lines of 
battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Pakistan (2806):

  435th   
  Lt Cav  
