 325th/A  
  Legion  
          
  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 436th Light Cavalry in reserve.  Standing at the 
ready with his warriors was Josh the gentle Sevenhalf-eight.  Rutger marched 
with his loyal troops, jaws set in grim determination.
  As luck would have it, Josh the gentle's formations were partially hidden 
by a sudden mist, giving them a small edge.  Also, Josh the gentle's clever 
tactical maneuvers assured his forces an undeniable advantage.

  Across the entire front, the Veteran 358th Warg Riders were accompanied by 
a band of the Order of Black Knights, who whipped them into a fanatical 
terror with their rabid battle lust.  They were arrayed against the 325th 
Legion.  The 352nd Light Cavalry outflanked the undermanned enemy and 
charged in with full force.  The 358th Warg Riders battled with the 325th 
Legion and trampled them down as if they were invalids.
  The forces of Josh the gentle broke through and were victorious.  The 
358th Warg Riders demolished the 325th Legion.
  Pakistan was overrun by Josh the gentle's men in a hard-fought campaign.  
The battle affected the quality of our forces:  we can raise the ranking of 
the 352nd Light Cavalry to Veteran, its officers having displayed great 
courage.  Josh the gentle's experience raised his skill in Tactics.
  In late summer, Josh the gentle spoke urgently to Rutger and convinced him 
to pledge his services to Josh the gentle.  After talking to Rutger, 
Josh the gentle judged him (a Dwarf famous for Marches) to have an Evil, 
Berserk nature.
  The summer surrendered to a colorful fall.  Josh the gentle moved into 
Kara-Kum (#2805) with his redoubtable army.  Viewing the western horizon, a 
man can see a rich Mountain province called Persia (#2705).  It is said that 
Neferititi is the ruler there.  It is known to be occupied by Humans.  Their 
Human fighters array themselves in the style of Legion and Chariots.  To the 
northwest there lies a Sea province known as the Caspian Sea (#2704), a 
prosperous area of no races where no one reigns.  Josh the gentle discovered 
a Monastery (#174) in Kara-Kum, occupied by the Titan.  What treasure may 
lie there is unknown.  Priests revere the Titan as a godlike being which 
occasionally visits the material plane of existence.  They are tremendously 
powerful, and it is fortunate that they are usually of good alignment.

  A conquering horde owing their allegiance to 
Josh the gentle Sevenhalf-eight invaded the province of Kara-Kum, a Desert 
area ruled by Mannanan (#104).  Josh the gentle was in command of the 
attacking armies.  The defending forces were led by Mannanan.  The armies 
were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Kara-Kum (2805):

  435th   
  Lt Cav  
