  DEFENDING ARMY

  The attackers had the 436th Light Cavalry in reserve.  
Josh the gentle Sevenhalf-eight stood ready at the head of his thousands.  
Mannanan led his armies courageously into the fray.
  Josh the gentle's soldiers, ill-supplied in the desert campaign, suffered 
from thirst.  Mannanan's soldiers, with no camels in the desert, suffered 
from thirst.  Josh the gentle's luck took a turn for the better when his 
advance guard located and occupied a high rock outcropping, which was well 
suited as an observation post.  Further, his clever tactical maneuvers 
assured his forces a clear advantage.

  Across the whole front, the Veteran 352nd Light Cavalry were accompanied 
by a company of the Order of Black Knights, who whipped them into a 
fanatical terror with their rabid battle lust.  They were arrayed against 
the 324th Bowmen.  The 358th Warg Riders and the 435th Light Cavalry flanked 
the undermanned enemy lines and attacked with full strength.  The 352nd 
Light Cavalry fought the 324th Bowmen and squashed them like rotten oranges.
  The battle ended victoriously for the soldiers of Josh the gentle as they 
broke through at a critical moment.  The 352nd Light Cavalry annihilated the 
324th Bowmen.
  Kara-Kum was overrun by the forces of Josh the gentle.  The battle 
affected the quality of our forces:  the fun head-bashing by the 358th 
Warg Riders during the battle has raised the morale of its warriors, and all 
agree that it has achieved Crack quality.
  During early winter, Josh the gentle could not hire Mannanan because there 
wasn't enough gold to pay Mannanan.

  Thus endeth the adventures of Josh the gentle Sevenhalf-eight for this 
year.


  Josh the gentle Treated with Stoqaxoqtl, but Stoqaxoqtl did not react 
favorably to his amicable noises.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings 
will see the wisdom of Treating.
  Josh the gentle Treated with Shauku Endbringer, but Shauku did not react 
to his friendly noises.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings will see the 
wisdom of Treating.
  Josh the gentle Treated with Tumijin Khaan, but Tumijin Khaan did not 
react to his friendly noises.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings will 
see the wisdom of Treating.
  Josh the gentle Treated with Lord Avalanche, but Avalanche did not react 
to his friendly overtures.  It is hoped that next year, both Kings will see 
the wisdom of Treating.

  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  York (#67) has arrived in Kara-Kum from Karaganda.
  Urians (#228) heard tales of fine hunting in Hindu Kush and left Pakistan 
to take a vacation there.


  Here is the financial report for Josh the gentle's kingdom: this turn, the 
Kingdom collected 59 gold in revenue.  3 gold was expended to finance our 
leaders.  The 445th Fleet and the 446th Bowmen trained well and improved in 
quality.  25 gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Josh the gentle was 
left with 31 gold in the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Managgen
To: Josh the gentle

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I travelled to Rajasthan.
  With the coming of the early summer season, I recruited enough men in 
Rajasthan to create the 445th Fleet for the army of Managgen.
  Midsummer's day passed and late summer came.  I sailed into the Arabian 
Sea (#2807) with my formidable forces.
  Managgen's naval forces took possession of the Arabian Sea practically 
uncontested.  The Arabian Sea was discovered to have an income of 2 gold.
  During fall, I moved into the Ind. Ocean 2808 (#2808) with my 
high-spirited Fleet.
  Managgen's forces conquered the Ind. Ocean 2808 without any major battles. 
The Ind. Ocean 2808 was found to have a tax base of 3 gold.
  With the coming of the early winter season I cast a Bless spell.  India 
was magically blessed and prospered.  The Bless affected no armies in India.

  Thy humble servant,   Managgen


From: Herlen
To: Josh the gentle

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Winter gave way to spring.  I boldly marched my forces into Chungking 
(#106).

  An army coming from the empire of Josh the gentle Sevenhalf-eight invaded 
Chungking, hoping to conquer that province owned by the provincial Eagle 
chieftain and made up of extensive Mountains.  I commanded the invading 
armies.  The defenders were commanded by the provincial Eagle chieftain.  
The armies were drawn up into lines of battle as shown here:

  ATTACKING ARMY, Battle of Chungking (0106):

  429th   
  Axemen  
