IMPERIAL OFFICE REPORT

  Into thy heroic dreams cometh an apparition heaven-sent, to speak to thee of
thy progress in thy ambitions for Imperial Office.  It is not for mortal Kings
to know who rivals them for high offices, but the Divine One will allow you to
know thy place in the standings, and how thee compares to thy fiercest foreign
rival for each office (shown under "Riv%" as a percentage: your points divided
by your rival's points, times 100.)

Imperial Office           Best Hope     Rank  Riv%   Second Hope   Rank  Riv%
World Emperor             Josh the gentle  1   129   None
  An ethereal Emerald Crown appeared on Josh the gentle's head, and a 
booming voice heard only by Josh the gentle ordained "This is the Crown of 
the Emperors of the Ancient Dynasty which ruled this world thousands of 
years ago.  It is yours for as long as you are the best hope to become the 
next World Emperor, and can be given to no other.  The Crown will give you 
the ability to know the strength of all your rivals in your quest for 
Empire".  (This information will be shown in your Diplomacy report in future 
gameturns).  Only the tax bases of kings bordering your kingdom that you 
have known for at least one full turn will be shown.

Esteemed High Chancellor  Josh the gentle 16    42   Managgen        26    28
Imperial Treasurer        Josh the gentle  2    91   None
Imperial Grand Marshal    Josh the gentle  1   125   None
  As Josh the gentle reviewed his troops in parade, he was startled by the 
sudden appearance of a Silver Baton in his right hand.  A gruff voice which 
only Josh the gentle seemed to hear commanded, "You are to have the 
guardianship of this Marshal's Silver Baton, handed down from the Imperial 
Grand Marshals of the Ancient Dynasty who kept order in the Empire untold 
years ago, in an almost-forgotten era.  It will allow you to recruit one 
extra unit of any army type which can move overland (except for flying 
units).  For example, if a province has Legion and Chariot army types, you 
may recruit two of each type.  The Baton cannot be transferred, and will 
remain yours only for as long as you remain the world's greatest general".

Imperial Grand Admiral    Rutger          10    33   Herlen          10    33
Lord High Defender        Rutger           4     0   Herlen           4     0
High Priest Palatine      Managgen         2    90   Josh the gentle   4    80
Arch-Mage Palatine        Herlen          20    40   Managgen        20    40
King of Pain              Josh the gentle  1   307   None
Praetorian Guard          358th Orc Wargs  1   107   None
  The title of "Praetorian Guard" is reserved for the military land unit 
best suited to serve as the imperial palace guard for the emperor.  The 
title is worth 2 prize percentage points on the Imperial Office Table.
  As the Praetorian Guard, the 358th Warg Riders has won recognition as the 
land unit most qualified to protect the future World Emperor.  Whenever they 
encamp with other armies, they spend their time telling stories of the great 
battles they have fought.  Their gallantry inspires their fellow soldiers to 
train more intensively, so that when the 358th Warg Riders trains other land 
units, their chance to improve in quality is doubled, and the chance for 
non-land units is increased by half.


  The Evil alignment now controls 6% of the world's votes
(taxbase + (5 X office/treasure points)).     


